# P2. the overshoot mechanism, and whether a tight formula exists

## Q1. is the overshoot confined to degenerate operands?

### mul_full
   NON-degenerate operands : tight 1098, overshoot 127
   at least one degenerate : tight 1, overshoot 70
   first NON-degenerate overshoot: U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(1, 1), least U(0, 1)

### add_mixed
   NON-degenerate operands : tight 1175, overshoot 50
   at least one degenerate : tight 0, overshoot 71
   first NON-degenerate overshoot: U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(2, 1), least U(1, 1)

### sub_mixed
   NON-degenerate operands : tight 715, overshoot 510
   at least one degenerate : tight 36, overshoot 35
   first NON-degenerate overshoot: U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(1, 1), least U(0, 1)

## Q2. the mechanism, for whichever site still overshoots

### mul_full: 127 non-degenerate overshoots
   integer-width excess values : [1]
   fraction-width excess values: [0]
   every least answer equals (I1, max(F1,F2)) : False
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(1, 1), least U(0, 1)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 1) -> formula U(1, 2), least U(0, 2)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 2) -> formula U(1, 3), least U(0, 3)

### add_mixed: 50 non-degenerate overshoots
   integer-width excess values : [1]
   fraction-width excess values: [0]
   every least answer equals (I1, max(F1,F2)) : False
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(2, 1), least U(1, 1)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(2, 0) -> formula U(3, 1), least U(2, 1)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(3, 0) -> formula U(4, 1), least U(3, 1)

### sub_mixed: 510 non-degenerate overshoots
   integer-width excess values : [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
   fraction-width excess values: [0]
   every least answer equals (I1, max(F1,F2)) : True
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 0) -> formula U(1, 1), least U(0, 1)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 1) -> formula U(1, 1), least U(0, 1)
   e.g. U(0, 1) , U(1, 2) -> formula U(1, 2), least U(0, 2)

